<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Jesus Prayer</span><span class="sg-chain-h">prayer that grew out of the phrase</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Musical settings of the Mass ordinary</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the Kyrie is their first sung movement</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Psalms 6:2, 9:13, 31:9, 86:3 and 123:3 (Septuagint)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the phrase</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gospel of Matthew 15:22, 17:15 and 20:30</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the same plea made to Jesus</span></li></ul></section>
